    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18440" root="زون" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُونٌ</span></b>  <i>An idol:</i> and <i>anything that is taken as a
deity and worshipped,</i> (S, K, * TA,) <i>beside God:</i>
as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُورٌ</span>: [an arabicized word:] in Pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">Cُونْ</span>.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>A place in which idols are collected and set up.</i> (K.) It is said to be from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِينَةٌ</span>. (TA.) [But it may rather be from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُونَةٌ</span> as
a dial. var. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِينَةٌ</span>.] ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِوَنٌّ</span>.

